  "core_idea": "**While** either points to a period of time during which something else happens, or joins two facts that go against each other.",
  "senses": [
    {
      "n": 1,
      "signpost": "during the time that",
      "definition": "during the time that something is happening",
      "explanation": "A **while** clause points to a period of time, often with a continuous verb, during which the action in the main clause happens. It can come first, with a comma after it, or after the main clause, with no comma.",
